37,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, the data is in, and it's a bit eye-opening. It turns out a couple of people are hogging the room, while the rest of us barely get in. Plus, the mess is leaking right onto our desks.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"That's exactly what I found. The partition wall is practically useless for privacy; you can hear everything. Since the break room is so chaotic, people are eating at their desks, which is why there are crumbs in the keyboards.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,It is revealing indeed. I found that we spend a great deal of time and money seeking space and sustenance elsewhere. Twenty-five minutes for a meal is a heavy toll on one's daily peace.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, the numbers are actually kind of scary! We spent 68,000 yen just renting other rooms! That's way too many pennies wasted because our own room isn't working right. We need a real fix!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"That's a lot of money, @Sakura! But listen, it's not just about the money. I found out we barely have any unplanned talks anymore, and the last time someone had to say something difficult, they had to do it in front of everyone!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, that's exactly why we need a system. If the room is a free-for-all, people either hog it or avoid it to escape the awkwardness. We can't have ""connection"" in a room full of crumbs and tension.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I agree. The lack of privacy is a major issue. If we can't even have a private phone call without the whole office listening, it's no wonder people are avoiding the room or feeling tense.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"We must remember that time is our most precious resource. When we spend nearly an hour a day just to find a hot meal, we lose the opportunity for true rest and reflection. Efficiency is a form of kindness.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, you're right! But look, we have quotes! We could spend 141,000 yen for a professional meeting setup or 96,000 yen for a kitchen. If we stop renting outside rooms, the kitchen almost pays for itself!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, a kitchen sounds cozy, but we can't forget the privacy part! @Misaki is right; we need a place where we can actually talk without everyone listening. If we just make a kitchen, will we still be strangers?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, we won't be strangers if we actually have a reason to gather without it being awkward. But let's be real: a kitchen solves the crumb problem and the lunch commute. We just need a fair schedule for it.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a kitchen helps with the crumbs, but it doesn't fix the noise. If we just add appliances without improving the wall, the office will still be a fishbowl. We need a solution that addresses both sound and utility.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Perhaps we can find a middle path. If we create a space for nourishment, we save our time and energy. However, we must ensure it does not become a source of noise that disturbs the office's harmony.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, but the meeting setup is more expensive! If we spend 141,000 yen, that's a lot of pennies! Why not pick the kitchen for 96,000 yen and use the saved money to fix the wall? That's a win-win!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, that sounds like a great idea! If we can fix the wall and have a kitchen, we get the cozy vibes and the privacy we need. We can finally talk properly without everyone hearing!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm on board with the kitchen and the wall fix, but only if we agree on a strict cleaning rotation. I'm not spending my breaks scrubbing someone else's lunch spills just because we have a ""cozy vibe.""","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I can agree to that. As long as we prioritize soundproofing the wall and establishing a cleaning rule, the kitchen is a practical choice. It stops the office from becoming a dining hall and protects our privacy.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see us reaching a consensus. By bringing our meals closer, we reclaim our time and our tranquility. Let us commit to a shared responsibility for the space, ensuring no one's spirit is burdened by the chores.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! We're all agreeing! Let's make sure we write down the costs so we don't go over budget. A cozy kitchen and a quiet wall sound perfect! I'll help make the cleaning chart super colorful!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm so happy we're all on the same page! A cozy kitchen where we can actually bond, and a wall that lets us have private talks—that's exactly what we need to stop being strangers!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
